Week-13 
IAM Roles

# Procedure

## 1. Create IAM Role

1. Login to AWS Console → IAM → Roles → Create Role.
2. Select trusted entity as AWS Service.
3. Choose EC2 as the use case.
4. Attach permission policy `AmazonS3FullAccess`.
5. Enter role name and create the IAM role.

---

## 2. Launch and Configure EC2 Instance

1. Create and launch an EC2 instance.
2. Connect to the EC2 instance using SSH.
3. Verify AWS CLI command:

   ```bash
   aws ec2 describe-instances
   ```

---

## 3. Attach IAM Role to EC2 Instance

1. Go to EC2 Dashboard and select the running instance.
2. Click Actions → Security → Modify IAM Role.
3. Select the created IAM role.
4. Click Update IAM Role.

---

## 4. Verify Role Permissions

1. Connect to the EC2 instance.
2. Run:

   ```bash
   aws s3 ls
   ```

   S3 buckets will be listed successfully.
3. Run:

   ```bash
   aws ec2 describe-instances
   ```

   Access will be denied because the role has only S3 permissions.

---

## Result

Successfully created and attached an IAM Role to an EC2 instance and verified temporary security credentials with restricted access permissions.
